The `isRefreshConnectionFlow` boolean flag controls if/else branching inside the `useEffect`. This flag is redundant — its effect on `headerTitleAddCards` (line 75) is dead code because when `feed` is provided (always the case from `RefreshCardFeedConnectionPage`), `headerTitle` takes the `feed` branch and ignores `headerTitleAddCards`. In the `useEffect`, the presence of `onRefreshComplete` already signals the refresh flow.

Remove `isRefreshConnectionFlow` and rely on `onRefreshComplete` as the signal:
```tsx
if (onRefreshComplete) {
    if (isFeedConnectionBroken) {
        updateBrokenConnection();
    }
    onRefreshComplete();
    return;
}
```
Also remove the dead-code ternary in `headerTitleAddCards` at line 75, since it has no effect when `feed` is provided.

