The `wasSubmittedViaHarvesting` boolean flag prop controls an `if/else` branch inside the component body (line 80), switching between two distinct rendering strategies. This matches Case 1 of the rule: boolean flags that control feature presence or layout strategy within a component.

Moreover, this prop is redundant because the component already has enough information to derive this behavior: it parses `message` with `CONST.REGEX_ANCHOR_WITH_TEXT` to detect anchor tags. If the regex matches, the harvesting rendering path should be used. The component can own this decision internally rather than receiving a boolean flag from the parent.

Suggested fix: Remove the `wasSubmittedViaHarvesting` prop entirely and instead derive the rendering path from the `message` content:

```tsx
const messageSplitByAnchor = message.match(CONST.REGEX_ANCHOR_WITH_TEXT);

if (messageSplitByAnchor) {
    // Render the harvesting variant with parsed anchor parts
    const messagePrefix = messageSplitByAnchor.at(1) ?? '';
    const anchorHref = messageSplitByAnchor.at(2) ?? '';
    // ... rest of harvesting rendering
} else {
    // Render the default variant
}
```

This eliminates the boolean flag, removes a prop from the parent caller, and lets the component own its rendering behavior.

