The `todoItems` config array with `.filter()` and `.map()` is a Case 4 violation (config-array driven rendering). These are four statically-known items (submit, approve, pay, export) with distinct handlers and parameters, encoded as a data array and mapped through `BaseWidgetItem`. This PR extends the pattern by threading `singleReportIDs` into each item's handler, making the config objects more complex.

Consider refactoring each todo item into explicit JSX with conditional rendering instead of the config-array approach. This makes per-item navigation logic (single-report vs. search) more visible and avoids growing the config schema:

```tsx
<View style={styles.getForYouSectionContainerStyle(shouldUseNarrowLayout)}>
    {submitCount > 0 && (
        <BaseWidgetItem
            key="submit"
            icon={icons.Send}
            iconBackgroundColor={theme.widgetIconBG}
            iconFill={theme.widgetIconFill}
            title={translate('homePage.forYouSection.submit', {count: submitCount})}
            ctaText={translate('homePage.forYouSection.begin')}
            onCtaPress={createNavigationHandler(CONST.SEARCH.ACTION_FILTERS.SUBMIT, {from: [`${accountID}`]}, singleReportIDs[CONST.SEARCH.SEARCH_KEYS.SUBMIT])}
            buttonProps={{success: true}}
        />
    )}
    {approveCount > 0 && (
        <BaseWidgetItem
            key="approve"
            ...
        />
    )}
    {/* ...pay, export */}
</View>
```

Note: This config-array pattern predates this PR, but the new single-report navigation feature is being added through it, further expanding the config object shape.

