The `wasSubmittedViaHarvesting` boolean flag prop adds a configuration-driven rendering branch (Case 1). When `true`, the component renders a completely different message layout (`submittedVia` + `delaySubmissions` via TextBlock/TextLinkBlock) versus the default path that renders the `message` prop as a TextBlock. The `message` prop is also computed and passed but silently ignored in this branch.

Instead of a boolean flag, consider using composition so the caller controls the message content and the component remains stable. For example, accept `children` for the message portion and let the caller compose the appropriate content:

```tsx
// ReportActionItemMessageWithExplain accepts children for the message:
function ReportActionItemMessageWithExplain({children, action, childReport, originalReport}) {
    // ... existing actionHasReasoning logic ...
    return (
        <ReportActionItemBasicMessage>
            <View style={[styles.flexRow, styles.alignItemsCenter, styles.flexWrap]}>
                {children}
                {explainAndIconBlock}
            </View>
        </ReportActionItemBasicMessage>
    );
}

// Caller in PureReportActionItem.tsx composes the message:
children = (
    <ReportActionItemMessageWithExplain action={action} childReport={childReport} originalReport={originalReport}>
        <TextBlock textStyles={[styles.chatItemMessage, styles.colorMuted]} text={translate('iou.submittedVia')} />
        <TextLinkBlock onPress={() => openLink(CONST.SELECT_WORKFLOWS_HELP_URL, environmentURL)} style={[styles.chatItemMessage, styles.link]} text={translate('iou.delaySubmissions')} />
        <TextBlock textStyles={[styles.chatItemMessage, styles.colorMuted]} text=". " />
    </ReportActionItemMessageWithExplain>
);
```

This keeps `ReportActionItemMessageWithExplain` stable -- it always renders the message content (via `children`) plus the explain+icon block, and new message variants are handled at the call site without modifying this component.

